WEBVTT

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.297
Anything?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.637
Not really.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.838
The polyferranide deposits
are contaminated with astiline.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.869
Commander, there's
something over here

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:14.971
I think you should see.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.948
Pack it up.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.644
We'll find better quality
somewhere down the line.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.845
That line is going
to be cut short

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.513
when our nacelles
burn themselves up

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.748
if we don't find it soon.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.347
What have you got, Lieutenant?

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.451
There have been other visitors
to this moon recently.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.485
What do you think this is?

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.860
Some kind of message?

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.002
I don't want you
to go wandering off.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.569
I'm not.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.172
I'm just looking at something.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.308
Antonio.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.218
Vay-chit no-op-puse-nee.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.347
Chakotay, kay-nee-post.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.254
Pon-ah-chee nun-pah-hee-no.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.692
Kay-nee-post itchee-oh.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.753
Kep-pon-nee!

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.162
He says you're quite a scout.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.859
A kep-pon-nee.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.892
I was just looking at a lizard
when I saw it.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.733
Well, it was your eyes
that saw it.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.738
No one else's did.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.967
That's the important thing.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.202
Come.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.301
I want you to understand this.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.976
It's a blessing to the land.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:26.484
An ancient healing symbol.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.248
A CHAH-mooz-ee.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:31.519
They probably cut this down
for firewood.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.423
The Rubber Tree people?

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.258
Well, the closest thing to
the Ancient Rubber Tree people

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.661
that we'll ever see.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:40.825
The people in this tribe
are their descendants.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.027
Just like we are.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.264
But they never left this jungle.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.138
And they rarely intermarry
with other tribes.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.870
And they still use firewood
instead of magnesite fuel

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.877
like everyone else.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:55.312
Chakotay, they've chosen

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.679
to live like this for centuries.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.183
That's why we are traveling
on foot

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.845
and not using a transporter.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.013
We honor the Sky Spirits

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.616
who led our ancestors
to this sacred land.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.319
Sacred land?

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.349
Yes.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.691
Huh.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.256
The Sky Spirits must have taken
a wrong turn somewhere.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.745
Maybe it's
a blessing to the land.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.975
For damaging it
with the campfire.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:33.280
What is your basis
for that conclusion, Commander?

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.721
Oh, just...

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.657
something somebody told me once.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.404
Describe the nature
of your pain.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.931
In the lower back.

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.273
It's tight.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.575
Choose the word that would
best describe your pain.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.547
Burning, throbbing, piercing,

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.880
pinching, biting,
stinging, shooting...

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:45.884
Shooting.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.579
It even goes down my legs.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.609
Hmm.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.679
Is the baby all right?

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:51.849
Hmm? Oh, certainly.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.654
Fine, nothing to worry about.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.854
Well, that makes me feel better.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:56.919
The position of the baby

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.988
is simply putting pressure
on your sciatic nerve.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.090
You may return to your post.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:05.900
The pain makes it difficult
to sit for any period of time.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.462
It's really quite uncomfortable.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.065
Elevating your legs when you sit

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.939
should provide
all the relief you need.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:13.568
Perhaps a day of rest, off-duty.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.602
Mm-mm.

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.376
Ensign Wildman, according
to your medical history,

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.214
this is your first pregnancy,
correct?

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.720
Yes.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.221
Well, Ensign, unfortunately,
pregnancy causes

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.223
its fair share of discomforts

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.656
and you'll have
to learn to live with them.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.158
That's just the way it is.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.218
We'll schedule her
for follow-up in two days.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:31.423
If the pain has not subsided
on its own by then,

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:32.522
we'll attempt to decrease

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.465
the sensitivity
of the nerve in that region.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.797
Thank you, Doctor.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:43.237
Call me day or night
if this gets any worse.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.976
Don't you have any compassion
for the way she feels?

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.141
Every member of this crew
is an adult.

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:53.981
I will not coddle them.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.580
Compassion can be
your department.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.886
Fortunately, you have
enough for both of us.

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:01.553
You've never been
sick or in pain.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:04.222
I just wish, once in your life,
you could know what it's like,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.525
how it makes you
feel vulnerable

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:06.532
and a little afraid.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:08.193
Then you'd understand.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:15.266
I don't have a life.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.799
I have a program.

00:06:23.981 --> 00:06:25.949
I hated every minute of it.

00:06:26.017 --> 00:06:28.508
My father had dragged me
all the way from our colony

00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:31.317
near the Cardassian border
on this quest of his.

00:06:31.355 --> 00:06:35.485
Away from my friends, my home,
and here we were, in the middle

00:06:35.526 --> 00:06:37.494
of a brutal Central
American jungle

00:06:37.528 --> 00:06:39.928
looking for the descendants
of the Ancient Rubber people.

00:06:39.964 --> 00:06:42.125
It must have been
very important to him.

00:06:42.166 --> 00:06:43.258
Believe me, it was.

00:06:43.301 --> 00:06:44.290
And he was very disappointed

00:06:44.335 --> 00:06:46.826
that I didn't
share his enthusiasm.

00:06:46.871 --> 00:06:49.669
He'd been tracking down the
origins of our tribe for years.

00:06:53.044 --> 00:06:55.979
The one on the right
is the one I found today.

00:06:56.047 --> 00:07:00.609
And now, something you saw
on that trip years ago,

00:07:00.651 --> 00:07:02.881
shows up again
on a moon surface

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.582
almost 70,000 light-years away.

00:07:08.826 --> 00:07:10.521
I don't suppose
you have any theories

00:07:10.561 --> 00:07:12.426
that might explain this.

00:07:13.831 --> 00:07:14.889
I can give you

00:07:14.932 --> 00:07:17.025
an official Rubber Tree
people theory if you like.

00:07:18.903 --> 00:07:23.033
- Sky Spirits.
- Sky Spirits?

00:07:23.074 --> 00:07:24.564
It's an ancient myth.

00:07:24.609 --> 00:07:27.908
Sky Spirits from above
created the first Rubber people

00:07:27.945 --> 00:07:30.539
in their own image,
and led the way to a sacred land

00:07:30.581 --> 00:07:32.742
where the Rubber people
would live for eternity.

00:07:32.783 --> 00:07:34.683
You obviously don't
put a great deal of faith

00:07:34.719 --> 00:07:36.277
in this explanation.

00:07:37.655 --> 00:07:39.953
How much faith do you put
in Adam and Eve?

00:07:40.024 --> 00:07:41.321
Hasn't science proved

00:07:41.359 --> 00:07:43.793
that all humans developed
from a single

00:07:43.828 --> 00:07:44.954
evolutionary process?

00:07:44.996 --> 00:07:46.896
That's what I was always taught.

00:07:46.931 --> 00:07:48.956
On the other hand,
none of my teachers

00:07:49.066 --> 00:07:51.534
ever spent much time
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:07:52.703 --> 00:07:54.295
B'Elanna tells me we picked up

00:07:54.338 --> 00:07:56.465
a warp signature
heading away from the moon.

00:07:56.507 --> 00:07:58.065
Think we should follow it?

00:07:58.109 --> 00:07:59.337
I don't know that it's fair
for me

00:07:59.377 --> 00:08:03.211
to put my own personal curiosity
ahead of the ship's priorities.

00:08:03.247 --> 00:08:05.044
We still haven't found
the polyferranide

00:08:05.082 --> 00:08:06.549
we need to seal the warp coils.

00:08:06.584 --> 00:08:09.553
If these people have warp
technology, they might be able

00:08:09.587 --> 00:08:10.645
to help us.

00:08:13.858 --> 00:08:15.416
Besides...

00:08:15.459 --> 00:08:18.792
we are in the business
of exploring, aren't we?

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.458
My father would put on
his expedition hat

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.933
and shout, "Let's go!"

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:25.936
I guess that's
good enough for me.

00:08:38.082 --> 00:08:39.879
Showing no life signs.

00:08:39.917 --> 00:08:41.942
Mr. Paris, are you certain
the warp signature ended here?

00:08:41.986 --> 00:08:43.647
Positive, Captain.

00:08:44.989 --> 00:08:46.320
Harry, check your sensors.

00:08:46.357 --> 00:08:49.417
That look like some kind
of power source to you?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.758
That is an unusually
high EM reading

00:08:51.796 --> 00:08:53.457
for a natural occurrence.

00:08:53.497 --> 00:08:55.294
Could be some kind
of cloaking technology.

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:59.463
Mr. Kim, transmit a continuous
message on all frequencies

00:08:59.503 --> 00:09:01.403
identifying who we are,
where we're from

00:09:01.439 --> 00:09:03.134
and make it clear
our intentions are peaceful.

00:09:03.174 --> 00:09:04.141
Torres to Bridge.

00:09:04.175 --> 00:09:05.142
Go ahead.

00:09:05.176 --> 00:09:06.302
We're in luck, Captain.

00:09:06.344 --> 00:09:08.312
My readings are showing
high concentrations

00:09:08.346 --> 00:09:10.906
of polyferranide about ten
kilometers below the surface.

00:09:11.015 --> 00:09:11.913
Acknowledged.

00:09:12.016 --> 00:09:14.007
We'll send out an away team
to continue the survey.

00:09:14.051 --> 00:09:15.518
Report to Transporter Room 3.

00:09:15.553 --> 00:09:16.611
On my way.

00:09:16.654 --> 00:09:18.588
Commander,
if we meet any resistance

00:09:18.622 --> 00:09:19.589
abort the mission.

00:09:19.623 --> 00:09:21.386
I have no intention
of disturbing an alien race

00:09:21.425 --> 00:09:22.653
that would rather be left alone.

00:09:22.693 --> 00:09:23.660
Understood.

00:09:23.694 --> 00:09:26.356
On the other hand,
if we can make contact, our goal

00:09:26.397 --> 00:09:29.127
is to get permission to begin
excavation as soon as possible.

00:09:29.166 --> 00:09:30.793
Tuvok, you're with me.

00:09:30.835 --> 00:09:33.929
Mr. Neelix, please report
to Transporter Room 3

00:09:33.971 --> 00:09:35.302
for an away mission.

00:09:35.339 --> 00:09:36.966
I'll meet you there, Commander.

00:09:41.178 --> 00:09:42.907
We may be out of luck.

00:09:42.947 --> 00:09:44.244
Problem?

00:09:44.281 --> 00:09:45.908
I'm not sure
we can transport down.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.850
Every time we try
to lock on to a transport sight,

00:09:47.885 --> 00:09:48.909
a storm begins.

00:09:48.953 --> 00:09:50.580
Storm?

00:09:50.621 --> 00:09:53.351
We've tried seven different
sites and as soon as we lock on,

00:09:53.391 --> 00:09:55.382
an electrical storm forms
right above the location.

00:09:55.426 --> 00:09:56.723
When we change sites,

00:09:56.761 --> 00:09:58.786
a new storm forms
and the old one dissipates.

00:09:58.829 --> 00:10:00.763
Might the transporter
beam itself

00:10:00.798 --> 00:10:03.392
be causing an electrostatic
charge in the atmosphere?

00:10:03.434 --> 00:10:05.061
That's as good a guess as any.

00:10:05.102 --> 00:10:06.729
I can't explain it.

00:10:06.771 --> 00:10:08.739
We just can't transport.

00:10:08.773 --> 00:10:10.400
Fine, we'll take a shuttle.

00:10:19.517 --> 00:10:21.382
Once again, the storm
seems to have formed

00:10:21.419 --> 00:10:22.386
as a direct result

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.115
of our interaction
with the atmosphere.

00:10:24.155 --> 00:10:26.385
The meteorological
conditions changed radically

00:10:26.424 --> 00:10:28.415
when we began
our entry sequence.

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:30.393
Shields are holding.

00:10:33.631 --> 00:10:35.792
It takes more
than a little thunderstorm

00:10:35.833 --> 00:10:38.996
to bother one of your mighty
Starfleet ships, huh?

00:10:39.036 --> 00:10:41.004
Nothing we can't handle.

00:10:41.038 --> 00:10:42.232
Relax, Neelix.

00:10:54.652 --> 00:10:57.212
That's why they call it
a rain forest.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:03.153
Why do your Sky Spirits
choose a place where it rains

00:11:03.194 --> 00:11:04.752
all the time?

00:11:04.795 --> 00:11:06.922
And it's hot...

00:11:06.964 --> 00:11:08.488
and there are so many bugs?

00:11:10.634 --> 00:11:14.070
It's said the Sky Spirits
honored the land above all else.

00:11:15.673 --> 00:11:17.664
Maybe it's because this land

00:11:17.708 --> 00:11:20.370
yields so many
different kinds of life.

00:11:20.411 --> 00:11:24.108
Maybe they wanted us
to become friends

00:11:24.148 --> 00:11:25.979
with everything in nature.

00:11:26.016 --> 00:11:27.483
Including the bugs.

00:11:27.518 --> 00:11:28.576
Sorry, Sky Spirits.

00:11:28.619 --> 00:11:30.678
I will never make friends
with bugs.

00:11:32.857 --> 00:11:35.052
Maybe that's why
they keep biting you.

00:11:38.496 --> 00:11:39.793
You're miserable.

00:11:41.966 --> 00:11:44.434
It was a mistake to bring you.
I'm sorry.

00:11:44.468 --> 00:11:49.064
I'm sorry I can't be
what you want me to be.

00:11:50.908 --> 00:11:53.502
From the day you came
out of your mother...

00:11:53.544 --> 00:11:55.569
upside down...

00:11:55.613 --> 00:11:59.208
I knew the spirits had
chosen you to be a contrary.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.184
No one chooses for me.

00:12:01.218 --> 00:12:03.345
I choose my own way.

00:12:03.387 --> 00:12:05.947
And if that makes me a contrary,

00:12:06.056 --> 00:12:07.683
I'll have to live with it.

00:12:07.725 --> 00:12:10.125
If you have no spirits
to guide you,

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.355
I fear you will lose your way.

00:12:17.668 --> 00:12:20.102
Altitude: 5,000 meters.

00:12:20.137 --> 00:12:22.970
Decreasing speed to 720 kph.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.668
Entering terminal
approach phase.

00:12:25.709 --> 00:12:27.404
Visibility still zero.

00:12:27.444 --> 00:12:29.503
Switching
to enhanced terrain scanning.

00:12:29.547 --> 00:12:31.572
Touchdown sight scanned.

00:12:31.615 --> 00:12:32.877
Continuing descent.

00:12:51.201 --> 00:12:54.932
Computer, activate the emergency
medical holographic program.

00:12:56.807 --> 00:12:59.002
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:12:59.043 --> 00:13:00.476
I thought we changed
your program

00:13:00.511 --> 00:13:02.706
so you wouldn't have
to say that anymore.

00:13:02.746 --> 00:13:03.838
We did.

00:13:03.881 --> 00:13:06.372
But I became so uncomfortable
trying to find new ways

00:13:06.417 --> 00:13:10.217
to "break the ice," as it were,
that I restored it.

00:13:10.254 --> 00:13:12.154
Let's just say it works for me.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.384
Doctor?

00:13:15.559 --> 00:13:17.493
Ah, you noticed.

00:13:17.528 --> 00:13:20.929
Are holograms
supposed to... sneeze?

00:13:20.965 --> 00:13:22.296
Generally, no.

00:13:22.333 --> 00:13:24.494
But I have accepted
your challenge.

00:13:24.535 --> 00:13:26.594
I programmed myself
with the symptoms

00:13:26.637 --> 00:13:28.264
of the 29-hour Levodian flu.

00:13:28.305 --> 00:13:30.296
Thus I will gain the experience

00:13:30.341 --> 00:13:31.968
that you suggest
would be beneficial

00:13:32.009 --> 00:13:33.476
to the performance of my duties.

00:13:36.113 --> 00:13:37.375
Holographic tissue paper

00:13:37.414 --> 00:13:39.109
for the holographic runny nose.

00:13:39.149 --> 00:13:40.707
Don't offer them to patients.

00:13:43.554 --> 00:13:45.988
Mmm, interesting sensation,
blowing one's nose.

00:13:46.056 --> 00:13:47.853
It's my first time.

00:13:47.891 --> 00:13:50.985
I think this is
very brave of you.

00:13:51.095 --> 00:13:52.289
Nothing of the sort.

00:13:52.329 --> 00:13:54.991
I intend it to be
an educational experience.

00:13:55.065 --> 00:13:56.828
I'm sure you'll learn a lot.

00:13:56.867 --> 00:13:58.835
I meant for the crew.

00:13:58.869 --> 00:14:02.703
I'm tired of the whiny,
cranky attitudes

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:03.934
we see around here.

00:14:04.041 --> 00:14:06.737
I intend to serve as an example
of how one's life and duties

00:14:06.777 --> 00:14:08.938
do not have to be disrupted
by simple illness.

00:14:08.979 --> 00:14:10.344
Doc?

00:14:10.381 --> 00:14:11.439
I don't feel so good.

00:14:11.482 --> 00:14:12.449
Neither do I,

00:14:12.483 --> 00:14:13.973
and you don't hear me
complaining.

00:14:22.559 --> 00:14:24.652
We are not making any progress
locating the source

00:14:24.695 --> 00:14:26.458
of that unusual power reading,
Commander.

00:14:27.798 --> 00:14:29.732
Then I guess we'll have
to search for these people

00:14:29.767 --> 00:14:31.632
the old-fashioned way...
with our eyes and ears.

00:14:31.669 --> 00:14:32.829
Is something bothering you,

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.064
Commander?

00:14:34.104 --> 00:14:36.937
No, it just reminds me

00:14:36.974 --> 00:14:38.965
of another jungle
that I visited once.

00:14:39.009 --> 00:14:41.534
The Central American rain forest
on Earth.

00:14:41.578 --> 00:14:43.307
It's the only other place
in the universe

00:14:43.347 --> 00:14:44.746
that I've ever seen this flower.

00:14:44.782 --> 00:14:48.218
It appears to be
a rare variety of Cypriprdium

00:14:48.252 --> 00:14:50.345
of the Asiatic genus
Paphiopedilum.

00:14:50.387 --> 00:14:52.116
I never knew you had

00:14:52.156 --> 00:14:55.717
such horticultural
expertise, Mr. Vulcan.

00:14:55.759 --> 00:14:58.956
In fact, I am...
or, more accurately, I was...

00:14:58.996 --> 00:15:00.987
a breeder of prize
Vulcan orchids.

00:15:02.132 --> 00:15:04.259
Then we have something
in common...

00:15:04.301 --> 00:15:05.268
I breed orchids, too!

00:15:07.204 --> 00:15:09.604
Don't they make
the most exquisite salad?

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:12.575
A touch of Baldoxic vinegar...
pure heaven.

00:15:12.609 --> 00:15:14.509
I hereby designate
the two of you

00:15:14.545 --> 00:15:16.536
the team's botanical surveyors.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.172
Collect a sample
of that flower.

00:15:18.215 --> 00:15:20.240
B'Elanna?

00:15:20.284 --> 00:15:23.253
It's just what we've
been looking for.

00:15:23.287 --> 00:15:24.811
Almost pure polyferranide.

00:15:24.855 --> 00:15:26.880
But there's a problem
with crust reactivity.

00:15:26.924 --> 00:15:28.414
If we can't solve it
before excavation,

00:15:28.459 --> 00:15:30.689
we might contaminate
the entire yield.

00:15:30.728 --> 00:15:33.390
Have Ensign Kim run an
analysis from the ship.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.692
We should be able to...

00:15:35.733 --> 00:15:37.701
I'll be damned.

00:15:37.735 --> 00:15:38.861
What?

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.830
It almost looks like a hawk,
doesn't it?

00:15:45.709 --> 00:15:47.074
Listen to him, Chakotay.

00:15:48.245 --> 00:15:49.576
What does he say to you?

00:15:52.649 --> 00:15:55.618
He says, "You are home."
Huh?

00:15:57.654 --> 00:15:59.747
I'm leaving the tribe, Father.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.223
What?

00:16:01.258 --> 00:16:04.819
I got to know a lot
of the Starfleet officers

00:16:04.862 --> 00:16:06.887
patrolling
the Cardassian border.

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:08.295
I asked Captain Sulu

00:16:08.332 --> 00:16:10.823
if he would sponsor me
at Starfleet Academy.

00:16:10.868 --> 00:16:12.062
And he would do such a thing

00:16:12.102 --> 00:16:13.626
without even
discussing it with me?

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:16.332
I told him I had your approval.

00:16:16.373 --> 00:16:17.340
Ah!

00:16:17.374 --> 00:16:19.535
I kept him as far away
from you as I could.

00:16:20.611 --> 00:16:23.603
I take it you've been
accepted by the Academy.

00:16:28.485 --> 00:16:31.386
Well, you've never
fully embraced

00:16:31.421 --> 00:16:33.946
the traditions of our tribe,
I know that.

00:16:34.057 --> 00:16:36.491
And you've always been curious
about other societies.

00:16:36.527 --> 00:16:39.826
And that is why I allowed you
to read about them.

00:16:39.863 --> 00:16:43.594
Because I believe that ignorance
is our greatest enemy.

00:16:43.634 --> 00:16:45.932
But to leave the tribe...

00:16:45.969 --> 00:16:47.869
Our tribe lives in the past.

00:16:47.905 --> 00:16:49.600
A past of fantasy and myth.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.801
That past is a part of you,

00:16:51.842 --> 00:16:54.367
no matter how hard
you try to reject it.

00:16:54.411 --> 00:16:57.642
Other tribes have learned
to accept the 24th century.

00:16:57.681 --> 00:16:58.875
Why can't ours?

00:17:01.585 --> 00:17:04.019
It is not the place
of a 15-year-old boy

00:17:04.054 --> 00:17:05.817
to question the choices
of his tribe.

00:17:05.856 --> 00:17:07.084
I know.

00:17:07.124 --> 00:17:08.489
That's why I have to leave.

00:17:08.525 --> 00:17:10.516
You will never belong
to that other life.

00:17:10.561 --> 00:17:13.394
And if you leave, you will
never belong to this one.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.796
You'll be caught between worlds.

00:17:15.833 --> 00:17:18.324
I ask for your blessing,
Father.

00:17:18.368 --> 00:17:20.165
Oon-day. Oon-day, Kolopak.

00:17:34.718 --> 00:17:37.915
Botanical surveyor number one
to Commander Chakotay.

00:17:37.955 --> 00:17:39.252
Go ahead, Neelix.

00:17:39.289 --> 00:17:40.950
You won't believe what I found.

00:17:41.058 --> 00:17:42.025
I think it's...

00:17:47.965 --> 00:17:48.954
Neelix, what the?

00:17:48.999 --> 00:17:50.967
The bird, the bird!

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.814
My eye!

00:18:04.848 --> 00:18:06.543
Away team to Voyager.

00:18:06.583 --> 00:18:07.550
Go ahead, Commander.

00:18:07.584 --> 00:18:09.051
Emergency beam-out.

00:18:09.086 --> 00:18:10.883
Get Neelix to Sick Bay.

00:18:10.921 --> 00:18:12.081
Acknowledged.

00:18:18.128 --> 00:18:19.288
Commander.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.701
You're very lucky this bird

00:19:01.738 --> 00:19:03.569
didn't snatch your eye
right out of the socket.

00:19:04.774 --> 00:19:07.004
We have no spare
Talaxian eyeballs.

00:19:07.043 --> 00:19:08.533
Is something
the matter with him?

00:19:08.578 --> 00:19:11.274
The Doctor gave himself
the Levodian flu

00:19:11.314 --> 00:19:12.508
to see what it's like.

00:19:12.549 --> 00:19:14.813
Is he contagious?

00:19:14.851 --> 00:19:16.716
It's a holographic simulation,
not an actual virus.

00:19:16.753 --> 00:19:18.414
There's no need for concern.

00:19:19.456 --> 00:19:20.548
You may sit up.

00:19:21.925 --> 00:19:22.892
Touchy, isn't he?

00:19:22.926 --> 00:19:24.223
He isn't feeling well.

00:19:24.261 --> 00:19:27.890
I don't require any compassion,
thank you very much.

00:19:27.931 --> 00:19:32.698
I have been experiencing these
symptoms for nearly 20 hours,

00:19:32.736 --> 00:19:36.069
and I am in complete command
of my faculties.

00:19:37.841 --> 00:19:40.275
You may both leave now.

00:19:57.661 --> 00:19:59.686
Mr. Kim believes
if we bombard the crust

00:19:59.729 --> 00:20:01.128
with antithoron radiation,

00:20:01.164 --> 00:20:03.826
we can decontaminate it
before excavation begins.

00:20:03.867 --> 00:20:05.960
Then all we need to do
is locate these people

00:20:06.036 --> 00:20:07.230
and get their permission.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.601
Any progress?

00:20:08.638 --> 00:20:09.969
Everything we've found here

00:20:10.073 --> 00:20:12.371
suggests the people
who live in this village

00:20:12.409 --> 00:20:13.774
left recently and in a hurry.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.142
Do you believe our arrival
frightened them?

00:20:16.179 --> 00:20:17.407
We can't discount that.

00:20:17.447 --> 00:20:19.312
You'd think
with warp technology,

00:20:19.349 --> 00:20:21.647
they would have encountered
other alien life before now.

00:20:21.685 --> 00:20:23.084
You'd think

00:20:23.119 --> 00:20:24.984
with warp technology, they
wouldn't be living like this.

00:20:25.021 --> 00:20:27.512
Captain, have you had
any unusual readings

00:20:27.557 --> 00:20:30.993
that might explain the images of
a strange face I've been seeing?

00:20:31.027 --> 00:20:32.551
Lmages?

00:20:32.595 --> 00:20:33.857
Very odd.

00:20:33.897 --> 00:20:35.660
Like the flash of a memory.

00:20:35.699 --> 00:20:37.758
But it's someone I've never met.

00:20:37.801 --> 00:20:40.964
Nothing unusual has shown up
on the ship's sensors.

00:20:41.004 --> 00:20:44.303
Tuvok hasn't detected
any telepathic activity, either.

00:20:44.341 --> 00:20:46.138
If you want to call it a day,
Commander...

00:20:46.176 --> 00:20:47.143
No.

00:20:47.177 --> 00:20:49.008
I think we'll press on
for a while.

00:20:49.112 --> 00:20:51.376
If there are any other problems,
I'll let you know.

00:20:51.414 --> 00:20:52.540
Chakotay out.

00:20:53.583 --> 00:20:56.211
The dwellings are constructed
with an alloy polymer matrix

00:20:56.252 --> 00:20:58.243
we've never encountered before,
Commander.

00:21:00.557 --> 00:21:01.956
They're out there.

00:21:01.992 --> 00:21:04.483
Our tricorders
may not tell us so,

00:21:04.527 --> 00:21:05.926
but they're out there.

00:21:13.203 --> 00:21:14.431
Lay down your weapons.

00:21:14.471 --> 00:21:15.460
Commander?

00:21:15.505 --> 00:21:17.439
Disarm... I want them to see

00:21:17.474 --> 00:21:19.135
that we don't pose
any threat to them.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:23.411
May I remind the Commander
that Starfleet protocol demands

00:21:23.446 --> 00:21:24.913
that away teams remain armed

00:21:24.948 --> 00:21:27.348
and ready to defend themselves
until contact is...

00:21:27.384 --> 00:21:29.716
I know all about
Starfleet protocol, Lieutenant.

00:21:29.753 --> 00:21:32.483
As we have not yet established
the inhabitants' intentions,

00:21:32.522 --> 00:21:34.387
it would not be
a logical course of action.

00:21:34.424 --> 00:21:37.484
The logical course
isn't always the right course.

00:21:37.527 --> 00:21:39.461
Lay down your weapons
in plain sight.

00:21:39.496 --> 00:21:40.463
Those are my orders.

00:21:40.497 --> 00:21:41.623
Would you at least permit me

00:21:41.664 --> 00:21:43.222
to advise the Captain
to move the ship

00:21:43.266 --> 00:21:44.893
into a stronger
tactical position?

00:21:44.934 --> 00:21:46.162
Negative.

00:21:46.202 --> 00:21:48.193
We'll show no force of any kind.

00:21:49.472 --> 00:21:53.340
For the record, I must take
exception to these orders.

00:21:53.376 --> 00:21:55.105
Noted.

00:22:02.052 --> 00:22:04.520
They have reason to be scared.

00:22:04.554 --> 00:22:06.454
Who can blame them?

00:22:06.489 --> 00:22:11.324
Their history, our history,
is filled with conquerors

00:22:11.361 --> 00:22:13.625
who brought slavery
and disease and death.

00:22:13.663 --> 00:22:15.631
Maybe we should
just leave them alone.

00:22:15.665 --> 00:22:22.969
Oh-chip way-nob-ee
teem-mock-uh an-tope-ah-nee.

00:22:23.073 --> 00:22:25.633
Hi-yeta-koo-nay-pas.

00:22:25.675 --> 00:22:30.237
Cha-kan-a hi-mee.
Cha-kan-a hi-mee.

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:32.874
Duh su kan-nuh-da.

00:22:34.784 --> 00:22:35.876
Binda kana.

00:22:38.188 --> 00:22:40.088
Binda kana.

00:22:46.262 --> 00:22:47.627
Father.

00:23:03.446 --> 00:23:05.471
Kah-yo-tay. Hay-noh.

00:23:53.096 --> 00:23:54.461
CHAH-mooz-ee.

00:24:40.677 --> 00:24:42.941
Teem-ma-ka-ha.

00:25:25.455 --> 00:25:27.821
I have no explanation,
Commander!

00:25:27.857 --> 00:25:30.417
There is no storm activity
indicated.

00:25:30.460 --> 00:25:32.894
All right, let's get back
to the shuttle.

00:25:48.911 --> 00:25:51.311
Hey! Wait!

00:25:58.454 --> 00:26:00.217
We will never make it!

00:26:00.256 --> 00:26:01.723
Where's Chakotay?!

00:26:01.758 --> 00:26:03.623
Away team to Voyager.

00:26:03.660 --> 00:26:05.093
Emergency beam-out.

00:26:24.212 --> 00:26:25.179
He was right behind us.

00:26:25.213 --> 00:26:27.181
I don't understand
what could have happened to him.

00:26:27.215 --> 00:26:29.683
Was he wearing the combadge
the last time you saw him?

00:26:29.718 --> 00:26:30.946
Just before the storm,
he was using it

00:26:30.986 --> 00:26:32.112
to speak with you, Captain.

00:26:32.153 --> 00:26:34.348
Mr. Paris, what are the current
surface conditions

00:26:34.389 --> 00:26:35.356
near the shuttle?

00:26:35.390 --> 00:26:37.517
Surface conditions are
back to normal, Captain.

00:26:37.559 --> 00:26:39.959
Winds two knots, but...

00:26:39.995 --> 00:26:41.690
I can't find any sign
of their shuttle.

00:26:41.730 --> 00:26:43.561
It's not where they landed it.

00:26:43.598 --> 00:26:44.860
And it isn't airborne?

00:26:44.899 --> 00:26:46.161
No, ma'am.

00:26:46.201 --> 00:26:47.190
I'll lead the away team back.

00:26:47.235 --> 00:26:48.600
Mr. Tuvok, Lieutenant,
you're with me.

00:26:48.636 --> 00:26:49.967
Mr. Paris, you have...

00:26:50.005 --> 00:26:51.973
Captain Janeway,
this is the Doctor.

00:26:52.007 --> 00:26:55.135
Please turn to your emergency
medical holographic channel.

00:26:57.746 --> 00:26:59.213
What is it, Doctor?

00:26:59.247 --> 00:27:01.181
Something terrible has happened.

00:27:01.216 --> 00:27:02.183
My program...

00:27:03.918 --> 00:27:05.408
Doctor, I think you're carrying

00:27:05.453 --> 00:27:08.081
this experiment of yours
a little too far.

00:27:08.123 --> 00:27:10.887
One hour too far, to be precise.

00:27:10.925 --> 00:27:14.656
I very specifically programmed
a 29-hour Levodian flu.

00:27:14.696 --> 00:27:17.597
And it has now been 30 hours.

00:27:17.632 --> 00:27:19.725
Doctor, I'm sorry, but we have
more pressing matters...

00:27:19.768 --> 00:27:20.860
You can't leave me like this.

00:27:20.902 --> 00:27:22.870
I need help, now!

00:27:22.904 --> 00:27:24.303
Get me somebody
who can tweak the computer

00:27:24.339 --> 00:27:25.863
and make me feel better,
immediately.

00:27:28.610 --> 00:27:29.599
Very well.

00:27:30.612 --> 00:27:32.239
Mr. Kim is on his way.

00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:33.713
Try to relax, Doctor.

00:27:33.748 --> 00:27:35.613
I'll see to that, Captain.

00:27:35.650 --> 00:27:37.083
I'm going to need you
with me, Kes.

00:27:37.118 --> 00:27:38.710
Prepare a medkit
and bring it with you

00:27:38.753 --> 00:27:39.720
to Transporter Room 3.

00:27:39.754 --> 00:27:41.187
Commander Chakotay
is still on the surface

00:27:41.222 --> 00:27:42.189
and may be injured.

00:27:42.223 --> 00:27:43.190
Janeway out.

00:27:46.461 --> 00:27:49.396
Oh, I don't understand it.

00:27:49.431 --> 00:27:52.628
I... I ran
a computer diagnostic

00:27:52.667 --> 00:27:56.262
and it said
that my program was fine.

00:27:56.304 --> 00:27:58.670
Just rest, Doctor.

00:27:59.941 --> 00:28:02.341
Here's a cool,
holographic towel

00:28:02.377 --> 00:28:03.639
for your forehead.

00:28:03.678 --> 00:28:04.770
Oh, thank you.

00:28:04.813 --> 00:28:05.802
Thank you so much.

00:28:05.847 --> 00:28:07.542
Please...

00:28:07.582 --> 00:28:08.674
don't go yet.

00:28:08.716 --> 00:28:09.910
I have to.
The Captain...

00:28:09.951 --> 00:28:13.887
I feel like I'm fading,
just... fading away.

00:28:13.922 --> 00:28:15.913
You don't know what that means
to a hologram.

00:28:15.990 --> 00:28:17.651
What seems to be the problem?

00:28:18.893 --> 00:28:24.229
My simulated virus is leading me
to a simulated death.

00:28:24.265 --> 00:28:25.254
It's nothing to worry about.

00:28:25.300 --> 00:28:27.598
I just added a couple of hours
to his computer program.

00:28:27.635 --> 00:28:31.401
He'll be fine
in about 45 minutes.

00:28:32.907 --> 00:28:34.067
Knowing when it would end

00:28:34.109 --> 00:28:36.907
didn't exactly make it
a fair test, did it, Doctor?

00:28:45.386 --> 00:28:50.153
Oh, she is far more devious
than I ever suspected.

00:29:39.207 --> 00:29:41.038
No shuttle.

00:29:41.075 --> 00:29:43.441
Well, at least
they got out okay.

00:30:03.765 --> 00:30:05.995
You have nothing
to fear from me.

00:30:07.735 --> 00:30:09.498
Talk to me.

00:30:09.537 --> 00:30:10.868
Let me see you.

00:31:06.861 --> 00:31:08.795
Is-to ko-hee-nis.

00:31:08.830 --> 00:31:10.092
No!

00:31:10.131 --> 00:31:11.359
Thank you.

00:31:49.304 --> 00:31:52.034
You have nothing
to fear from me.

00:31:53.875 --> 00:31:55.206
Talk to me.

00:31:56.210 --> 00:31:57.643
Let me see you.

00:32:19.834 --> 00:32:20.801
I don't understand it.

00:32:20.835 --> 00:32:22.063
It's the same thing
that happened

00:32:22.103 --> 00:32:23.434
the first time
we tried to go down.

00:32:23.471 --> 00:32:26.167
A storm develops wherever
we try to lock on.

00:32:26.207 --> 00:32:27.538
Why would we have the ability

00:32:27.575 --> 00:32:29.736
to beam people up,
but not to beam them down?

00:32:29.777 --> 00:32:30.869
I believe

00:32:30.912 --> 00:32:33.278
we have seen enough
to discern a pattern, Captain.

00:32:33.314 --> 00:32:34.679
The logical conclusion is

00:32:34.716 --> 00:32:36.616
that someone is controlling
the elements of nature

00:32:36.651 --> 00:32:37.879
to ward us off.

00:32:37.919 --> 00:32:40.615
The transporter anomaly is
evidence of this conclusion.

00:32:40.655 --> 00:32:42.646
We are allowed
to leave the planet,

00:32:42.690 --> 00:32:43.782
but not to approach.

00:32:43.825 --> 00:32:45.486
If that's true, I'd be happy

00:32:45.526 --> 00:32:47.892
to respect their wishes,
but, unfortunately,

00:32:47.929 --> 00:32:50.193
I have a missing crewman
to get back first.

00:32:50.231 --> 00:32:51.289
Janeway to Paris.

00:32:51.332 --> 00:32:52.629
Yes, Captain.

00:32:52.667 --> 00:32:54.601
Mr. Paris, we're going to land
Voyager on the surface.

00:32:54.635 --> 00:32:56.000
Take us into the atmosphere.

00:32:56.104 --> 00:32:58.004
Acknowledged.

00:32:58.039 --> 00:32:59.597
Beginning entry sequence.

00:33:11.419 --> 00:33:13.683
I'm reading electrical storms
forming all around us.

00:33:13.721 --> 00:33:15.552
Adjusting flight path.

00:33:15.590 --> 00:33:18.388
The barometric pressure
is continuing to fall.

00:33:18.426 --> 00:33:21.156
We're looking
at monsoon conditions out there.

00:34:02.336 --> 00:34:04.065
Mr. Paris, the shuttle crew
didn't report

00:34:04.105 --> 00:34:05.936
turbulence this severe
during their landing.

00:34:06.040 --> 00:34:07.598
I'm doing the best I can,
Captain.

00:34:07.642 --> 00:34:10.236
I'm showing gale force
winds out there.

00:34:10.278 --> 00:34:11.677
It is conceivable
that the aliens

00:34:11.712 --> 00:34:13.543
have been able
to intensify their response

00:34:13.581 --> 00:34:15.674
now that they are familiar
with our capabilities.

00:34:16.851 --> 00:34:17.875
Red Alert!

00:34:17.919 --> 00:34:19.853
Inertial dampers are off-line.

00:34:21.155 --> 00:34:22.884
We seem to be caught
in some kind of vortex.

00:34:22.924 --> 00:34:25.256
I can't maintain altitude.

00:34:25.293 --> 00:34:26.453
Captain, it's a cyclone.

00:34:39.974 --> 00:34:41.737
Altitude 20,000 meters
and falling.

00:34:41.776 --> 00:34:43.937
I can't get us out
of this thing, Captain.

00:34:43.978 --> 00:34:44.945
Bridge to Torres.

00:34:44.979 --> 00:34:46.947
We need more power
from the engines.

00:34:46.981 --> 00:34:48.972
I've got them running 20 percent
over rated maximum, Captain.

00:34:49.083 --> 00:34:50.710
It's not enough.

00:34:50.751 --> 00:34:52.742
Could we go to low warp
under these conditions?

00:34:52.787 --> 00:34:54.880
The ship might make it
without inertial dampers,

00:34:54.922 --> 00:34:57.322
but we'd all just be stains
on the back wall.

00:34:58.526 --> 00:34:59.993
I can try to augment the engines

00:35:00.027 --> 00:35:02.154
with power from the auxiliary
fusion reactors,

00:35:02.196 --> 00:35:04.221
but it's going to take
at least 20 minutes.

00:35:04.265 --> 00:35:06.358
How much time do we have,
Mr. Paris?

00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:08.459
Altitude at 18,000 meters
and falling.

00:35:08.502 --> 00:35:10.936
At this rate, we're looking
at about ten minutes.

00:35:37.531 --> 00:35:39.556
If you can hear me, speak to me.

00:35:44.238 --> 00:35:46.297
Dosh-du-pah kee-ne?

00:35:46.340 --> 00:35:50.242
Swasge-muh kee-say-yo-pah?

00:35:50.277 --> 00:35:51.904
Swas-ti-ma-hay.

00:35:51.946 --> 00:35:53.743
Kee-say-yo-pah.

00:35:53.781 --> 00:35:57.808
Pah-kee-ne?
Sas-ga no-yo-du no-kay-dah?

00:35:57.852 --> 00:35:59.820
I'm sorry.

00:35:59.854 --> 00:36:02.846
I don't know the ancient
language of my people.

00:36:02.890 --> 00:36:05.450
I can't understand.

00:36:05.493 --> 00:36:08.792
Po-kud-zee yo-atah.

00:36:08.829 --> 00:36:10.763
Pon-tez-butz-su.

00:36:19.240 --> 00:36:20.468
A CHAH-mooz-ee.

00:36:22.009 --> 00:36:23.840
CHAH-mooz-ee.

00:36:25.179 --> 00:36:28.512
Swasge-muh kee-say.

00:36:30.785 --> 00:36:33.686
Yo-pah no-kay-dah?

00:36:42.363 --> 00:36:44.126
CHAH-mooz-ee.

00:36:54.608 --> 00:36:56.633
Altitude 6,000 meters.

00:36:56.677 --> 00:36:59.874
Warning. Approach vector
is too steep.

00:36:59.914 --> 00:37:02.007
Discontinue landing sequence.

00:37:02.049 --> 00:37:04.415
Would somebody
turn that off, please?

00:37:04.452 --> 00:37:05.680
Engineering, report.

00:37:05.720 --> 00:37:08.018
We need that extra power,
B'Elanna.

00:37:08.055 --> 00:37:09.852
Ten minutes.

00:37:09.890 --> 00:37:12.882
I just need ten minutes!

00:37:22.403 --> 00:37:24.837
Do you understand my words now?

00:37:26.207 --> 00:37:27.196
Yes.

00:37:27.241 --> 00:37:29.505
Explain the face marking.

00:37:29.543 --> 00:37:32.103
I wear it to honor my father.

00:37:32.146 --> 00:37:34.637
He wore it
to honor his ancestors.

00:37:34.682 --> 00:37:36.650
Ancestors...

00:37:36.684 --> 00:37:37.946
You are human?

00:37:38.052 --> 00:37:38.950
Yes.

00:37:39.053 --> 00:37:41.886
Are there others
on your world with this mark?

00:37:41.922 --> 00:37:42.946
Yes.

00:37:42.990 --> 00:37:44.753
Not many, but some.

00:37:44.792 --> 00:37:46.953
We were taught all of them
had been annihilated.

00:37:47.061 --> 00:37:50.326
We were taught
your world had been ravaged

00:37:50.364 --> 00:37:53.856
by those with no respect
for life or land.

00:37:53.901 --> 00:37:56.335
There was a time
when that was true.

00:37:56.370 --> 00:37:58.167
But no longer.

00:37:59.306 --> 00:38:02.207
He claims to be a descendent
of the Inheritors.

00:38:03.310 --> 00:38:04.572
Inheritors?

00:38:08.849 --> 00:38:12.216
The ones...
our ancestors chose to honor.

00:38:12.253 --> 00:38:14.915
I'm surprised you have no memory

00:38:14.989 --> 00:38:16.923
of the Inheritors.

00:38:16.991 --> 00:38:19.824
One of our gifts
was the memory.

00:38:19.860 --> 00:38:23.261
If you are a descendent,
you should remember.

00:38:25.232 --> 00:38:28.030
I'm not sure I understand.

00:38:28.068 --> 00:38:31.094
Perhaps it has
been lost over time.

00:38:34.375 --> 00:38:36.866
45,000 years ago,

00:38:36.911 --> 00:38:39.675
on our first visit
to your world,

00:38:39.713 --> 00:38:42.648
we met a small group
of nomadic hunters.

00:38:42.683 --> 00:38:44.844
They had no spoken language,

00:38:44.885 --> 00:38:48.753
no culture, except the use
of fire and stone weapons,

00:38:48.789 --> 00:38:51.952
but they did have
a respect for the land

00:38:52.059 --> 00:38:56.826
and for other living creatures
that impressed us deeply.

00:38:56.864 --> 00:38:59.230
We decided
to give them an inheritance...

00:38:59.266 --> 00:39:01.166
a genetic bonding...

00:39:01.202 --> 00:39:04.660
so they might thrive
and protect your world.

00:39:04.705 --> 00:39:08.300
On subsequent visits,
we found that our genetic gift

00:39:08.342 --> 00:39:11.573
brought about a spirit
of curiosity and adventure.

00:39:11.612 --> 00:39:14.479
It impelled them to migrate
away from the cold climate

00:39:14.515 --> 00:39:17.143
to a new, unpeopled land.

00:39:17.184 --> 00:39:19.015
It took them almost
a thousand generations

00:39:19.053 --> 00:39:20.748
to cross your planet.

00:39:20.788 --> 00:39:23.916
Hundreds of thousands of them
flourished in their new land.

00:39:23.991 --> 00:39:26.050
Their civilization
had a profound influence

00:39:26.093 --> 00:39:28.152
on others of your species.

00:39:28.195 --> 00:39:31.289
But then new people came
with weapons

00:39:31.332 --> 00:39:33.027
and disease.

00:39:35.002 --> 00:39:37.835
The Inheritors who survived
scattered.

00:39:37.872 --> 00:39:40.466
Many sought refuge
in other societies.

00:39:40.507 --> 00:39:42.805
12 generations ago
when we returned,

00:39:42.843 --> 00:39:45.607
we found no sign
of their existence.

00:39:45.646 --> 00:39:49.707
My people called you
the Sky Spirits.

00:39:52.386 --> 00:39:55.617
Why have you been hiding from us
since we landed here?

00:39:55.656 --> 00:39:57.624
When we heard your message,

00:39:57.658 --> 00:40:01.150
who you were, observed
you probing our land,

00:40:01.195 --> 00:40:03.459
we believed you were a threat.

00:40:03.497 --> 00:40:05.556
We thought you
would annihilate us

00:40:05.599 --> 00:40:06.759
as you had the Inheritors.

00:40:06.800 --> 00:40:10.133
Our message was supposed to
communicate peaceful intentions.

00:40:10.170 --> 00:40:12.138
We were taught that is the way

00:40:12.172 --> 00:40:14.970
human conquerors
often introduce themselves.

00:40:15.075 --> 00:40:17.509
As I said...

00:40:17.544 --> 00:40:19.307
we've tried to change our ways

00:40:19.346 --> 00:40:21.405
since the last time
you stopped by.

00:40:25.219 --> 00:40:26.982
Altitude: 2,000 meters.

00:40:27.054 --> 00:40:28.282
Stand by, Bridge.

00:40:28.322 --> 00:40:30.790
We're initiating
the transfer now.

00:40:30.824 --> 00:40:33.588
I'm showing an eight percent
boost in the engines.

00:40:33.627 --> 00:40:35.424
That's all?

00:40:35.462 --> 00:40:36.986
The fusion reactors
are nearly drained.

00:40:37.064 --> 00:40:39.555
Fighting the storm is taking
every reserve we have.

00:40:39.600 --> 00:40:41.431
Altitude: 1,000 meters.

00:40:41.468 --> 00:40:43.231
Impact in 20 seconds.

00:40:43.270 --> 00:40:44.601
B'Elanna.

00:40:46.206 --> 00:40:48.106
Impact in 15 seconds.

00:40:48.142 --> 00:40:51.236
I'm sorry, Captain,
that's all we've got.

00:40:54.348 --> 00:40:56.077
Impact in ten seconds.

00:41:02.790 --> 00:41:04.087
Report.

00:41:04.124 --> 00:41:05.955
We're free.

00:41:06.060 --> 00:41:07.584
Gaining altitude.

00:41:07.628 --> 00:41:09.926
2,000 meters.

00:41:09.964 --> 00:41:13.127
2,500.
Dampers back on line.

00:41:13.167 --> 00:41:16.102
The storms have
completely dissipated.

00:41:16.136 --> 00:41:19.264
There's not a cloud in the sky.

00:41:23.344 --> 00:41:24.936
Stand down Red Alert.

00:41:24.979 --> 00:41:28.210
Anybody have an explanation?

00:41:28.248 --> 00:41:29.806
It appears the inhabitants
of this planet

00:41:29.850 --> 00:41:31.545
have decided to make contact,
Captain.

00:41:31.585 --> 00:41:33.712
The cloaking device
has been turned off,

00:41:33.754 --> 00:41:36.689
and we are showing
an alien population.

00:41:36.724 --> 00:41:38.851
I have located the shuttle.

00:41:38.892 --> 00:41:40.985
It may be possible
to locate Commander Chakotay

00:41:41.061 --> 00:41:42.187
without landing.

00:41:43.597 --> 00:41:45.656
Establish a search pattern,
Mr. Paris.

00:41:45.699 --> 00:41:46.666
Yes, Captain.

00:41:46.700 --> 00:41:48.258
Begin scanning
for human life signs.

00:41:48.302 --> 00:41:51.931
As soon as you find Chakotay,
we'll send down an away team.

00:41:56.410 --> 00:41:58.605
My ship will be coming
for me soon.

00:41:58.645 --> 00:42:00.943
I'm sorry we cannot permit you

00:42:00.981 --> 00:42:03.848
to extract all the materials
you need.

00:42:03.884 --> 00:42:07.081
You were generous
to offer as much as you did.

00:42:08.722 --> 00:42:10.622
You have a long journey ahead.

00:42:10.657 --> 00:42:13.057
It took us
more than two generations

00:42:13.093 --> 00:42:15.425
to reach your world.

00:42:21.235 --> 00:42:23.931
I wish I could see
my father's face right now.

00:42:23.971 --> 00:42:25.802
Does he still live?

00:42:27.741 --> 00:42:29.003
No.

00:42:31.178 --> 00:42:32.509
He died fighting enemies

00:42:32.546 --> 00:42:34.571
who would have
taken our home colony.

00:42:34.615 --> 00:42:37.607
Our tribe moved there
a few hundred years ago.

00:42:37.651 --> 00:42:42.384
So he honored the land
just as... his ancestors did.

00:42:44.391 --> 00:42:45.915
Yes.

00:42:45.959 --> 00:42:47.586
Yes, he did.

00:42:51.198 --> 00:42:54.656
We weren't on very good terms
when he died.

00:42:54.701 --> 00:42:56.760
Once he was gone, I didn't know

00:42:56.804 --> 00:42:58.999
how to reconcile
our differences,

00:42:59.039 --> 00:43:01.337
how to heal our old wounds.

00:43:01.375 --> 00:43:03.104
I returned to my colony,

00:43:03.143 --> 00:43:05.441
and continued the fight
in his name.

00:43:05.479 --> 00:43:09.279
I took the mark that he wore
to honor his ancestors.

00:43:09.316 --> 00:43:12.581
I spoke to him
in my vision quests,

00:43:12.619 --> 00:43:15.850
but he never answered.

00:43:15.889 --> 00:43:17.720
Until now.

00:43:38.879 --> 00:43:40.574
CHAH-mooz-ee.

00:43:45.419 --> 00:43:46.181
Commander.

00:43:51.492 --> 00:43:53.289
Put those away.

00:44:14.248 --> 00:44:17.513
Listen to him, Chakotay.

00:44:17.551 --> 00:44:20.315
Do you hear
what he says to you?

00:44:20.354 --> 00:44:22.481
Yes, Father.

00:44:22.523 --> 00:44:23.854
I hear him.

00:44:26.560 --> 00:44:28.425
I finally hear him.

00:44:46.013 --> 00:44:47.844
Four to beam up, Voyager.
